# ~/.claude -- the agent governance layer, under version control.
#
# THIS IS AN ALLOW-LIST. Line 1 ignores everything. Every `!` below re-admits one thing on
# purpose. A file nobody has thought about is therefore EXCLUDED by default, which is the
# only arrangement that survives a session dropping a key somewhere new.
#
# Do not convert this to a deny-list. The reason is measured, not stylistic: ~/.claude is
# written by every session on this machine, so the set of files here changes daily and no
# deny-list stays complete for a week.

*

# Every `!` line below is anchored with a leading `/`. Without it, `!README.md` admits a
# README.md at ANY depth, not the one at the root -- which is how docs/README.md became
# tracked the moment a docs/ tree appeared. In an allow-list, an unanchored name is a hole
# that opens later, when someone creates a directory nobody was thinking about.

# --- the laws and the operating rules -------------------------------------------
# AGENTS.md is the single source as of 2026-08-21 (founder instruction). CLAUDE.md is the
# eleven-byte line `@AGENTS.md` that imports it, because Claude Code 2.1.238 does not read a
# user-scope AGENTS.md on its own -- a fresh session with the laws in AGENTS.md alone answered
# NOT PRESENT when asked to quote one. Both files are tracked: this .gitignore denies everything
# at line 11, so leaving AGENTS.md off this list would leave the ONLY copy of the 17 laws
# untracked and unrecoverable.
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
# Both of the above are symlinks to ~/AGENTS.md now, so git holds 12 bytes
# of path and none of the law text. This is where the text lives.
!/AGENTS.snapshot.md
!/README.md
!/.gitignore

# --- the guards: this is the part that actually refuses things ------------------
!/scripts/
!/scripts/**/*.py
!/scripts/**/*.sh

# --- skills, directives, and the probes that answer "is it really live?" --------
!/skills/
!/skills/**
!/directives/
!/directives/**
!/state-probe/
!/state-probe/**

# --- projects/ is deliberately NOT here -----------------------------------------
# It held 878 checkpoint notes and 704 memory files: the founder's own words, the
# estate's infrastructure, and every conclusion six sessions ever reached. Founder,
# 2026-08-23: "this shold not be ingithub". It was removed from the index and from
# all 51 commits on that date. The files stay on disk and are backed up offsite;
# they do not go to a code-hosting vendor. Do not re-admit them with a `!` line and
# do not reach past this with `git add -f`.

# --- settings: the wiring that says which guard runs on which event -------------
# Tracked because an unwired guard refuses nothing, so the wiring IS governance.
# Scanned for secrets on every run of claude_repo.py before it may be committed.
!/settings.json

# --- never, under any circumstances, whatever a later ! line might say ----------
# These come last so they win. Credentials, keys, transcripts, and runtime state.
.credentials.json
**/.credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/keys/**
**/*token*.json
**/*secret*
**/*.jsonl
backups/

# The control plane's own config is NOT runtime state. A broad *.json rule above was
# swallowing lanes.json, which is the contract every lane field is declared in -- losing
# it loses the design, not a cache. Un-ignore by name, never by widening the rule.
!/lanes.json

# The laws evidence file: incidents, founder quotes, costs. Never injected, but must survive.
!/LAWS-INCIDENTS.md

# Written knowledge and shared records. These are what sessions are told to read and what the
# founder asked for; the allow-list was silently dropping them. Scanned for secret patterns
# before admission -- rescan before adding to this block.
!/DECISIONS.jsonl
!/ESTATE_BOARD.jsonl
!/ESTATE_COST_AUDIT_2026-08-06.md
!/ROLE_SET.md
!/TOKEN-FRAMEWORK.md
!/research/
!/research/**

# The agent definitions the Agent tool resolves by name, and the manifest saying
# which plugins this machine runs. Load-bearing, small, no secrets (LAW 24).
# The 85M plugins/cache stays out: it is a download, not a decision.
!/agents/
!/agents/**
!/plugins/
!/plugins/installed_plugins.json
!/plugins/known_marketplaces.json

# --- the dependency answer key ---------------------------------------------------
# Every external host and credential name this repository mentions is classified here as
# either covered by a drill or dismissed with a reason. It has to be tracked for the same
# reason AGENTS.md does: it is the only record of which vendors this estate decided it could
# survive losing, and drills/audit.py --sweep fails if the file is absent rather than reading
# a repository with no answer key as clean.
!/.dependencies.json
directives/.backfill-*

# --- LAW 22 evidence: the picture of the run -------------------------------------
# pr-evidence.py commits a screenshot of the proving run under docs/evidence/pr-<n>/,
# so the proof leaves with the code instead of living in GitHub's attachment store.
# Without these lines the pre-push evidence gate cannot be satisfied in this repository
# at all: line 11 ignores everything, `git add` refused, and the push stayed blocked.
#
# Admitted by extension, not by `**`. An image is opaque to a text secret scanner, so a
# blanket rule here would admit a file class nothing in this estate can read. Render the
# image from output you have already looked at.
!/docs/
!/docs/evidence/
!/docs/evidence/**/
!/docs/evidence/**/*.png
!/docs/evidence/**/*.md

# --- the pi-bridge executor: the MCP server, its fence tests and its cross-session primer --
# Untracked until 2026-08-27 (crew#513): the only copy of the executor lived in a working tree.
!/mcp/
!/mcp/*.py
!/mcp/*.md
